"item", "numeric-id": 749, "id": "Q749"}, "type": "wikibase-entityid"}, "datatype": "wikibase-item"}, "type": "statement", "id": "Q7927$F8758DAE-13EA-47B9-AFE9-DD72B476BB37", "rank": "normal"}], "P19": [{"mainsnak": {"snaktype": "value", "property": "P19", "hash": "0f5c235e51cb26df838888efea546f4b3b550db1", "datavalue": {"value": "Oh, no, the only person I really coached in the studio was Marilyn Monroe. I got that job through Jackie Mills who used to be a drummer with Tommy Dorsey, and he had an in with Jack Cole, the choreographer. So he took me out of the studio one day and Jack Cole liked what I did so every time Marilyn did a musical, I was there.", "type": "string"}, "datatype": "string"}, "type": "statement", "id": "Q7927$C58148CF-558A-4CDC-8941-B7925E53A651", "rank": "normal"}]}}